>
  <h2>What professional tax is</h2>
  <p>Professional tax is a small tax that the Constitution allows states and local bodies to levy on professions, trades, callings and employment. In Tamil Nadu it is collected by the local body where the person works or carries on business, under the Tamil Nadu Urban Local Bodies Act, 1998 and the Tamil Nadu Urban Local Bodies Rules, 2023. In Chennai that body is the Greater Chennai Corporation. Other corporations and municipalities in Tamil Nadu set their own rates, so the figures below apply only to the Chennai Corporation area.</p>
  <p>The Constitution caps professional tax at <strong>Rs 2,500 per person per year</strong>. Professional tax is separate from income tax: it is paid to the Corporation, not to the Income Tax Department.</p>

  <h2>Chennai professional tax slabs (per half-year)</h2>
  <p>The Greater Chennai Corporation revised the slabs from the half-year beginning October 2024, by its circular dated 20 January 2025. The tax is worked out on the salary or income for the half-year.</p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Half-yearly salary or income</th><th scope="col">Professional tax per half-year</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Up to Rs 21,000</td><td>Nil</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Rs 21,001 to Rs 30,000</td><td>Rs 180</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Rs 30,001 to Rs 45,000</td><td>Rs 425</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Rs 45,001 to Rs 60,000</td><td>Rs 930</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Rs 60,001 to Rs 75,000</td><td>Rs 1,025</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Above Rs 75,000</td><td>Rs 1,250</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p><strong>Example.</strong> An employee earning Rs 40,000 a month has a half-yearly salary of Rs 2,40,000, which is above Rs 75,000. The professional tax is Rs 1,250 for each half-year, or Rs 2,500 a year, the maximum. An employee earning Rs 6,000 a month has a half-yearly salary of Rs 36,000 and pays Rs 425 per half-year.</p>
  <p>Rates are revised from time to time by the Corporation council. Always check the latest demand notice or the Corporation's website before paying.</p>

  <h2>Who has to pay</h2>
  <ul class="checklist">
    <li><strong>Salaried employees</strong> working in Chennai whose half-yearly salary is above Rs 21,000. The employer deducts the tax from salary and pays it to the Corporation.</li>
    <li><strong>Employers</strong> with employees in Chennai must enrol with the Corporation, deduct professional tax from salaries and pay it on time.</li>
    <li><strong>Companies, firms and other businesses</strong> carrying on business in the Corporation area are assessed on their own account.</li>
    <li><strong>Self-employed professionals and traders</strong>, such as doctors, lawyers, consultants and shop owners, are also assessed by the Corporation.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Due dates</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Half-year</th><th scope="col">Due date</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>1 April to 30 September</td><td>By 30 September</td></tr>
        <tr><td>1 October to 31 March</td><td>By 31 March</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>Employers usually deduct the tax from salary during the half-year and pay it in one amount before the due date. Late payment attracts interest and penalty, which the employer bears where the tax was deducted from employees but not paid.</p>

  <h2>How to pay professional tax in Chennai online</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Go to the Greater Chennai Corporation website, <a href="https://chennaicorporation.gov.in/" rel="noopener">chennaicorporation.gov.in</a>, and open the professional tax section.</li>
    <li>Enter the professional tax assessment or registration number of the employer, business or individual.</li>
    <li>Check the half-year and the amount shown.</li>
    <li>Pay by net banking, debit card or credit card.</li>
    <li>Download and keep the receipt. Employers should keep a list of employees and the amount deducted from each for the half-year.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>New employers and businesses must first enrol with the Corporation to get an assessment number. Keep your trade licence, PAN and address proof ready.</p>

  <h2>Professional tax and your income tax return</h2>
  <p>Under the <strong>old tax regime</strong>, professional tax paid is deducted from salary income before working out taxable salary. Under the <strong>new tax regime</strong>, which is the default for individuals, this deduction is not available. Your Form 16 shows the professional tax deducted by your employer. Self-employed persons and businesses can generally claim professional tax paid as an expense. Compare both regimes using the <a href="/tools/it/">income tax calculator</a>.</p>

  <h2>Common mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Deducting professional tax at old rates after the October 2024 revision.</li>
    <li>Not enrolling as an employer when hiring the first employee in Chennai.</li>
    <li>Deducting from employees but paying late, which brings interest and penalty for the employer.</li>
    <li>Applying Chennai rates to staff working in another municipality, which has its own rates.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>For help with payroll compliance and returns, see <a href="/accounting-bookkeeping/">accounting and bookkeeping</a> and <a href="/income-tax-return-filing-chennai/">income tax return filing</a>.</p>
</Service>
